---
layout: layouts/page.njk
title: "Gyeonggi-do Population-Decline Counties"
description: "The Gyeonggi-do counties designated as population-decline or watch-list areas, which qualify for the F-1-D visa's lower, non-capital income threshold."
permalink: "/regions/gyeonggi-do/population-decline-counties/"
---
{# Not paginated like regions/region.njk — there's only one region this data can ever affect
   (architecture.md §7: Gyeonggi-do is the only capital-tier region, so it's the only place a
   population-decline county can change the eligibility outcome). Built the same way as a region
   page otherwise: same .content-page/.region-header shell, same .city-list pattern already used
   for cities.json entries (region.njk) reused here for county entries — same shape (English/
   Korean name + a category badge), just a different data source. #}
<div class="content-page content-page--tight-end">
<header class="region-header county-header">
  <h1>Gyeonggi-do population-decline counties</h1>
  <p class="region-header__intro">
    Gyeonggi-do is a capital-tier F-1-D region with the country's highest income threshold. Some
    counties — though administratively part of Gyeonggi-do — still qualify at the lower,
    non-capital threshold, because the government lists them as population-decline or watch-list
    areas.
  </p>
  <p class="region-header__intro">
    See the <a href="/visa-info/">visa info</a> for the rules and the
    <a href="/regions/gyeonggi-do/">Gyeonggi-do region page</a> for living info.
  </p>
</header>

{% macro countyCard(county) %}
{% set countyPhoto = countyHeroPhotos[county.countyNameEn] %}
{% set countyCredit = countyHeroCredits.photos[countyPhoto] %}
<li class="county-card">
  <div class="county-card__head">
    <h4 class="county-card__name">{{ county.countyNameEn }} <span class="county-card__ko">{{ county.countyNameKo }}</span></h4>
    <p class="county-card__metro">{{ county.metroEn }}</p>
  </div>
  {% if countyPhoto %}
  <figure class="county-card__figure">
    <img class="county-card__photo" src="/assets/img/hero/gyeonggi-do-population-decline/{{ countyPhoto }}" alt="{{ countyCredit.titleEn }}" loading="lazy">
    {% if countyCredit.titleEn %}
    <figcaption class="county-card__caption">
      <span class="county-card__caption-en">{{ countyCredit.titleEn }}</span>
      {% if countyCredit.titleKo %}<span class="county-card__caption-ko">{{ countyCredit.titleKo }}</span>{% endif %}
    </figcaption>
    {% endif %}
  </figure>
  {% endif %}
</li>
{% endmacro %}

<section class="region-section">
  <h2>Qualifying counties</h2>
  <p class="data-provenance">
    Source:
    <a href="https://www.mois.go.kr/frt/sub/a06/b06/populationDecline/screen.do">Ministry of the Interior and Safety (행정안전부) 인구감소지역 designation</a>,
    sourced 2026-08-18.
  </p>

  <div class="county-group">
    <h3 class="county-group__title">Population-decline-designated</h3>
    <ul class="county-grid">
      {% for county in populationDeclineAreas %}{% if county.category == "decline" %}{{ countyCard(county) }}{% endif %}{% endfor %}
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="county-group">
    <h3 class="county-group__title">Population watch-list</h3>
    <ul class="county-grid">
      {% for county in populationDeclineAreas %}{% if county.category == "watch" %}{{ countyCard(county) }}{% endif %}{% endfor %}
    </ul>
  </div>

  <p class="data-provenance">Photo source: © Korea Tourism Organization (한국관광공사).</p>
</section>
</div>
